# Losing all abilities to a resolved effect is a layer-6 effect too (CR 611.2, 613.1f), and layers 1 to 5 come first (CR
# 613.1, 613.6): Painter's Servant's "All cards that aren't on the battlefield, spells, and permanents are the chosen color in
# addition to their other colors" (layer 5) has applied by the time Oko, Thief of Crowns' +1 takes its abilities away, so Bot1's
# Island and Bot2's Mox stay blue. The Servant is a green Elk 3/3: Oko's "becomes green" is a later layer-5 effect and sets its
# color.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Painter's Servant
Island
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Island
Oko, Thief of Crowns
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Painter's Servant.Cast
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Colors = Blue
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Oko, Thief of Crowns.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Oko, Thief of Crowns.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Painter's Servant; Ability: Elk)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Painter's Servant.Colors = Green
Bot1.Battlefield.Painter's Servant.Subtypes = Elk
Bot1.Battlefield.Painter's Servant.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Colors = Blue
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Colors = Blue
Bot2.Battlefield.Oko, Thief of Crowns.Colors = Blue; Green
